    "narrative": "Our lineup today is anchored by high-floor contributors against favorable matchups, led by **Taylor Ward** (67.28) and **Luis Arraez** (67.31). **Taylor Ward** benefits significantly from a premier park factor (+16%), which, when paired with his leadoff positioning (+10%), makes him our most efficient offensive engine despite facing Canning. Meanwhile, **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman** (66.77) are poised to exploit the 4.63 xERA of Javier Assad. While the park conditions for that specific matchup are slightly suppressive (-3%), the platoon advantages and high-value spots in the batting order drive these projections into the high 60s. We are also capitalizing on **Gavin Sheets** (64.98), whose explosive park factor and platoon edge against Baz provide an elite ceiling for a player typically relegated to utility roles.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Bryson Stott** (48.48), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Bryson Stott** holds a favorable platoon edge against Misiorowski, his score was decimated by the opposing pitcher\u2019s elite skill profile (2.79 xERA), which effectively neutralized his base projection. Similarly, **Masyn Winn** (45.56) remained on the bench because he is running into a buzzsaw in Joe Ryan; even with a wind advantage, the matchup risk makes him a marginal start at best. Note that **Yainer Diaz** and **Cal Raleigh** remain unavailable due to IL status, leaving us thin behind the plate and increasing our reliance on the consistency of the current starters.\n\nManagement remains cautious regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Jonathan Aranda**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Drew Gilbert**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Matt Chapman**. With so much of our production tied to official lineup placement, any late-scratch or order-tweak could shift these efficiency scores drastically. **Geraldo Perdomo** (63.52) stands as a sneaky strong play today; his ability to overcome the 4.33 xERA of Lodolo through consistent contact and a positive platoon edge makes him a vital cog in our attempt to squeeze every possible point out of our 5x5 categories.",
